actBluetooth.description:
Allow operator to enable/disable Bluetooth interface.

        When actBluetooth is set to:

        enabled: Bluetooth interface is enabled;

        disabled: Bluetooth interface is disabled;

        autoFallback: Bluetooth is enabled automatically upon loss of connection to NetAct and disabled upon restoration of connection.

sspSecret.description:
Configure site-specific secret for Bluetooth secure simple pairing. The configured secret must be entered as a hex encoded string. For example, binary string 1mA is represented by hex encoding 316D41.

        If sspSecret is an empty string, a site-specific key, as derived from Nokia's default algorithm, will be used as the key for counter-based generation of a series of one time 6 digit passkey per RFC6238/RFC4226;

        If sspSecret is an non-empty string, Secure Simple Pairing Secret will be used as a key for counter-based generation of a series of one time 6 digit passkey per RFC6238/RFC4226.

extendedKeyUsage.description:
The parameter indicates one or more purposes for which the certified public key may be used, in addition to or in place of the basic
purposes indicated in the key usage. It is a string of IDs separated by space. RFC5280 specifies the meaning of the ID as following:
1: TLS WWW server authentiation;
2: TLS WWW client authentication;
3: Signing of downloadable executable code;
4: Email protection;
8: Binding the hash of an object to a time;
9 Signing OCSP responses;

keyUsage.description:
The parameter defines the purpose (e.g., encipherment, signature, certificate signing) of the key contained in the certificate. It is a bit string. When a bit is set to 1, it means the key usage corresponding to the bit applies to the certificate. In RFC5280, the meaning of the bits starting from the left-most is following: 
Bit 0: Digital Signature;
Bit 1: Content Commitment;
Bit 2: Key Encipherment;
Bit 3: DataEncipherment;
Bit 4: Key Agreement;
Bit 5: Key Certificate Sign;
Bit 6: Sign CRL;
Bit 7: Encipher Only; 
Bit 8: Decipher Only;

