maxNumCaConfUe.description:
Threshold to limit the maximum number of carrier aggregation configured UEs in a PCell (P-LNCEL); 
UEs may have 1 PCell (P-LNCEL) and 1 or several SCell(s) (S-LNCEL).
Carrier aggregated UEs with 1 or more SCell need more resources than nonCA Ues (PUCCH and MAC PS);
Therefore limiting the amount of CA-UEs is necessary.

In case the threshold is modified online and the value is decreased, existing CA-UEs may stay in the cell, but the new value applies to new admision checks only.

uLMeasHystJT.description:
Defines the hysteresis used on the threshold uLMeasJtCsiRs.
The hysteresis value is a function of uLMeasN and uLMeasAlphaBase.

A larger hysteresis value leads to a more stable UE location estimation at the cost of lower resolution.

It should be chosen such that the difference of 90th-percentile and 10th-percentile of the RSSI ratio estimate coresponds to twice the value of uLMeasHystJT. 

Example setup for >80% location estimates inside hysteresis range:
uLMeasN=75; uLMeasAlphaBase=0.013
@2GHz: uLMeasHystJT=2dB
@1GHz: uLMeasHystJT=2.6dB
@700MHz: uLMeasHystJT=3.3dB

uLMeasN=100; uLMeasAlphaBase=0.01
@2GHz: uLMeasHystJT=1.7dB
@1GHz: uLMeasHystJT=2.5dB
@700MHz: uLMeasHystJT=2.9dB

uLMeasHystSuMu.description:
